---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';

const principles = [
  ['No telemetry',        'Nothing phones home. The only network calls are to alert endpoints you configure yourself.'],
  ['No prompts stored',   'Guardrails read usage numbers and call metadata. Never transcripts, never credentials.'],
  ['Auditable in an afternoon', 'Zero runtime dependencies, pinned build deps, no postinstall scripts, npm provenance.'],
  ['Fails open on bugs',  'A crash inside the plugin must never take down the thing it protects.'],
];
---
<Base title="Open Source" og="open-source" description="Free, MIT-licensed guardrails for autonomous agents. No telemetry, no account, no network calls you didn't configure.">
  <section class="shell">
    <p class="eyebrow">Open source</p>
    <h1>Tools, given away</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      Everything here is MIT-licensed and free, including the parts that were annoying to
      build. A guardrail you cannot read the source of is not a guardrail.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="shell project-section">
    <article class="project">
      <div class="project__head">
        <h2>Belay</h2>
        <span class="tag" data-variant="live">v0.7.0</span>
        <span class="tag">MIT</span>
      </div>
      <p class="project__tagline">A seatbelt for OpenClaw agents.</p>

      <div class="project__body prose">
        <p>
          OpenClaw has no spend cap, no model-call rate limit, no cross-session budget and no
          graceful pause. The default agent runtime timeout is 48 hours. Belay is the layer
          that notices and steps in — gradually.
        </p>
        <pre><code>warn → block a tool call → end the run</code></pre>
        <p>
          Enforcement lands between calls, not mid-call. Your agent doesn't get killed; it
          gets caught, with its context intact.
        </p>
        <p>
          One caveat worth stating up front: the ladder's final rung — pausing the account
          outright — <strong>is not available on OpenClaw 2026.8.2</strong>, which refuses
          <code>channels.stop</code> from a hook handler. On that version the ladder tops out
          at ending the run.
        </p>
      </div>

      <dl class="specs">
        <div><dt>Guards</dt><dd>Spend caps, request-size limits, model-call and tool-call rate limits, identical-call limit, tool-error rate, pause ladder, flight recorder</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Runtime deps</dt><dd>Zero</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Requires</dt><dd>OpenClaw 2026.8.2+, Node 20+</dd></div>
      </dl>

      <div class="project__links">
        <a class="link-arrow" href="https://github.com/fathomforge/belay" rel="noopener">GitHub <span>&rarr;</span></a>
        <a class="link-arrow" href="https://www.npmjs.com/package/@fathomforge/belay" rel="noopener">npm <span>&rarr;</span></a>
      </div>

      <p class="disclaim">Not affiliated with the OpenClaw Foundation.</p>
    </article>
  </section>

  <section class="shell" aria-labelledby="h-principles">
    <h2 class="eyebrow" id="h-principles">How these are built</h2>
    <ul class="principles">
      {principles.map(([title, body]) => (
        <li>
          <h3>{title}</h3>
          <p>{body}</p>
        </li>
      ))}
    </ul>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  h1 { margin-bottom: .6rem; }
  .project-section { padding-top: 0; }
  .project {
    max-width: 820px;
    background: var(--bg-raised);
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    padding: clamp(1.5rem, 4vw, 2.5rem);
    box-shadow: var(--shadow);
  }
  .project__head { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: .8rem; flex-wrap: wrap; }
  .project__head h2 { margin: 0; }
  .project__tagline { color: var(--accent); margin: .35rem 0 1.4rem; }
  .project__body p { color: var(--fg-muted); }
  .project__body pre { font-size: .8rem; }

  .specs {
    margin: 2rem 0;
    padding: 1.5rem 0;
    border-block: 1px solid var(--line);
    display: grid;
    gap: 1rem;
  }
  .specs > div { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 10rem 1fr; gap: 1.25rem; }
  .specs dt {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: .74rem;
    letter-spacing: .08em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--fg-faint);
    padding-top: .18rem;
  }
  .specs dd { margin: 0; color: var(--fg-muted); font-size: .92rem; }

  .project__links { display: flex; gap: 1.75rem; }
  .disclaim { margin: 1.75rem 0 0; font-size: .8rem; color: var(--fg-faint); font-style: italic; }

  .principles {
    list-style: none; margin: 0; padding: 0;
    display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(215px, 1fr));
    gap: 2rem;
  }
  .principles h3 { font-size: 1.1rem; margin-bottom: .4rem; }
  .principles p { color: var(--fg-muted); font-size: .92rem; margin: 0; }

  @media (max-width: 600px) {
    .specs > div { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: .3rem; }
  }
</style>
